  "period_note": "Year-end position from the Annual Report's own 'Five Years Financial Summary' multi-year summary table (audited), Solo/Standalone basis. Reporting basis confirmed by matching this dataset's recorded Total Assets against the bank's own separate (Solo) Balance Sheet, which is consistently lower than its Consolidated Balance Sheet (the bank consolidates an Offshore Banking Unit and a brokerage subsidiary, SJIBL Securities Limited) -- directly verified in FY2013, FY2014, FY2020, FY2022 and FY2025 (see sources.json). As a Shariah-based Islamic bank, Shahjalal Islami Bank PLC reports 'Investment' rather than conventional 'Loans and Advances', and 'Classified Investment'/'Non-Performing Investment' rather than 'NPL', consistent with the convention used elsewhere in this dataset for EXIMBANK and FIRSTSBANK. Total Liabilities is not a separate line in the summary table and is calculated as Total Assets minus Total Shareholders' Equity. FY2025 report introduces an explicitly-labelled 'D) Consolidated Position' block within the same Five-Year Summary (Total Assets 429,466mn, Net Assets 25,902mn, PBT 8,676mn, PAT 3,681mn), plus a full separately-audited 'Consolidated Balance Sheet' (Total Property and Assets 429,466.29mn at line ~17481-17519, vs Solo 427,425.71mn at line ~17690-17742/Annexure-F) -- confirming the SOLO figures used throughout this dataset (427,426mn) remain consistent with the 14-year Solo convention. Independently cross-verified: the FY2022 Solo/Consolidated split found in the FY2022 report itself (Solo 339,818.87mn vs Consolidated 342,727.63mn) matches this FY2025 report's 'Consolidated Position' comparative for FY2022 (342,728mn) exactly.",
